{"role":"assistant","content":"The official Intervals.icu OAuth doc is revealing on two fronts:\n\n- The documented token response is exactly what Rivera got — `token_type`, `access_token`, `scope`, `athlete`, with **no `refresh_token` and no `expires_in`** (the doc's own example matches the log byte-for-byte in shape). Intervals tokens don't expire and there is no refresh flow — which explains why our server kills the connection after its invented 3600 s TTL.\n- The doc *does* list `CALENDAR: Planned workouts` as a valid scope family — so I need to double-check the current scope list (that announcement is from 2021; scopes may have changed). Let me check the newer integration cookbook:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_oLSK2SAT4AbromrJJq5FC0NC","function":{"name":"FetchURL","arguments":"{\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_gRONnl78RlnDN2jTEGpTVKKT","function":{"name":"WebSearch","arguments":"{\"query\":\"\\\"intervals.icu\\\" oauth scope \\\"EVENT:READ\\\" OR \\\"EVENT:WRITE\\\" OR \\\"CALENDAR:READ\\\"\"}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_gRONnl78RlnDN2jTEGpTVKKT","content":"Title: kuranov/intervals-icu-tools\nSite: Github\nDate: 2024-01-01\nURL: https://github.com/kuranov/intervals-icu-tools\nSnippet: Available OAuth scopes: ACTIVITY:READ , ACTIVITY:WRITE; WELLNESS:READ , WELLNESS:WRITE; CALENDAR:READ , CALENDAR:WRITE; SETTINGS:READ. Working with workout ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: I cannot find scope calendar:read and calendar:admin in the list of zoom scopes for OAuth App - API and Webhooks - Zoom Developer Forum\nSite: Zoom Developer Forum\nDate: 2024-06-04\nURL: https://devforum.zoom.us/t/i-cannot-find-scope-calendar-read-and-calendar-admin-in-the-list-of-zoom-scopes-for-oauth-app/111305\nSnippet: I cannot find scope calendar:read and calendar:admin in the list of zoom scopes for OAuth App API and Webhooks. I cannot find the certain ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: \nSite: Artisan Technology Group\nURL: https://www.artisantg.com/info/VDC_Display_Systems_8510_Manual_2017417121926.pdf?srsltid=AfmBOorElHR98GkBqASQiVQojFV6vUg_0ofexIvkvQnxRziO8ggaIJ8Z\nSnippet: The Interval Field The Interval field shows a date or interval at which the event is to take place. With the cursor positioned on the Interval field press[ENTER] to cycle through the available options. See Table 3-2 below for details. Table 3-2. Interval Field Options |EVENT INTERVAL|ACTIVATES THE EVENT|NOTES| |-|-|-| |specific date|At a specific calendar date|Use number keys for date entry per the format defined| |Daily|Every day.|| |Mon-Fri|Monday through Friday.|| |Sat-Sun|Saturday and Sunday\n\n---\n\nTitle: \nSite: Artisan Technology Group\nURL: https://www.artisantg.com/info/VDC_Display_Systems_8510_Manual_2017417121926.pdf?srsltid=AfmBOorHaCfDtacXSY-tvNTxoVocIcPexhwr5A3CYw84-zpXPpC9gMwa\nSnippet: The Interval Field The Interval field shows a date or interval at which the event is to take place. With the cursor positioned on the Interval field press[ENTER] to cycle through the available options. See Table 3-2 below for d