{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_NQ7so4jkbTc9v21FawPbpL1s","content":"The returned content is the main text extracted from the page. If you use it in your answer, cite this page as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url).\n\n## post by Sensitron on Jun 27, 2025\n\nIs a privacy policy mandatory when creating/requesting a new app? I just started developing and dont have one yet. Ofc i could just generate a dummy privacy policy i that is sufficent.\n\n## post by david on Jun 27, 2025\n\nNo you don’t have to start with one. Your app will start only visible to yourself. When you want all users to be able to see it then you need to have a privacy policy in place.\n\n13 days later\n\n\n## post by Sensitron on Jul 11, 2025\n\nHi David,\n\nSorry for being impatient. I sent you an email 11 days ago about the app integration, did you already see it?\n\n## post by david on Jul 11, 2025\n\nNo I didn’t see anything. Please resend to david@intervals.icu and I will sort it out right away.\n\n## post by Sensitron on Jul 11, 2025\n\ndone.\n\n1 month later\n\n\n## post by Mr\\_Jan\\_Exner on Aug 25, 2025\n\nHi David!\n\nCan I ask a question re Scopes? If I want to read athlete data (get /api/v1/athlete/{id}) and gear data (get /api/v1/athlete/{id}/gear{ext}), what scope do I need?\n\nI tried “ATHLETE:READ,GEAR:READ”, but neither exists.\n\nCheers,\n\nJan\n\n## post by david on Aug 25, 2025\n\nThese are the scopes: ACTIVITY, WELLNESS, CALENDAR, LIBRARY, SETTINGS\n\nYou need SETTINGS:READ for those.\n\n## post by Mr\\_Jan\\_Exner on Aug 25, 2025\n\nThanks, that helps!\n\nI can read the athlete, but I get a 405 if I try reading gear.\n\n\n![image1](https://kimi-web-img.kimi.ai/prod-data/online-image/search-upload/6d9196745d3d46ef00b197e6369dea48.png)\n\nWait… that seems to be my app, because on the documentation site it works, with the same access-token.\n\nI’ll try providing the athlete\\_id…\n\n## post by david on Aug 25, 2025\n\nThere isn’t an endpoint to get an individual bit of gear. You need to use the one that lists all gear for the athlete:\n\n```\nGET /api/v1/athlete/{id}/gear{ext}\n\n```\n\nYou can pass 0 for the athlete id.\n\n## post by Mr\\_Jan\\_Exner on Aug 25, 2025\n\nAh!\n\nAnd the documentation says that, too, urgh.\n\nThanks for your patience, David!\n\n1 month later\n\n\n## post by david on Sep 30, 2025\n\nOAuth apps can now subscribe to webhooks for chat messages and so on. Note that groups are also chats so this support includes group messages.\n\n\n![image2](https://kimi-web-img.kimi.ai/prod-data/online-image/search-upload/e4806956da2eb76d7570d0d3ae41f650.png)\n\nSample new message payload:\n\n```json hljs\n{\n  \"secret\": \"...\",\n  \"events\": [\n    {\n      \"athlete_id\": \"2049151\",\n      \"type\": \"CHAT_UPDATE\",\n      \"timestamp\": \"2025-09-30T07:18:59.147+00:00\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"type\": \"MESSAGES\",\n        \"chat_id\": 2741,\n        \"new_message_count\": 1,\n        \"messages\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": 2961313,\n            \"athlete_id\": \"xxx\",\n            \"name\": \"xxx\",\n            \"created\": \"2025-09-30T07:18:59.063+00:00\",\n            \"type\": \"TEXT\",\n            \"content\": \"bar\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n```\n\nSample new chat payload (another athlete has initiated a chat):\n\n```json hljs\n{\n  \"secret\": \"...\",\n  \"events\": [\n    {\n      \"athlete_id\": \"2049151\",\n      \"type\": \"CHAT_UPDATE\",\n      \"timestamp\": \"2025-09-30T07:22:59.005+00:00\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"type\": \"CHATS\",\n        \"chats\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": 1036589,\n            \"type\": \"PRIVATE\",\n            \"updated\": \"2025-09-30T07:22:58.986+00:00\",\n            \"name\": \"John xxx\",\n            \"picture\": \"https://...\",\n            \"pub\": false,\n            \"hide_members\": false,\n            \"members_cannot_chat\": false,\n            \"other_athlete_id\": \"xxx\",\n            \"other_athlete_sex\": \"M\",\n            \"role\": \"ADMIN\",\n            \"new_message_count\": 1,\n            \"last_seen_message_id\": 0\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n```\n\nCombine this with the chat endpoints to build Intervals.icu chat into your applications.\n\n## post by Mark\\_Boulton on Oct 1, 2025\n\nHi David - i’m building an OAuth integration for iOS and I continue to hit this error when trying to authenticate. I can confirm my details are correct when trying so, and i’m pretty stumped as to what is causing this. What is the ‘network error’ error raised for?\n\n\n![image3](https://kimi-web-img.kimi.ai/prod-data/online-image/search-upload/f86955bd7eb5ff29b211542731e1a144.jpeg)\n\n## post by david on Oct 1, 2025\n\nI don’t know what that is. Can you login from a normal Safari window?\n\n## post by Mark\\_Boulton on Oct 1, 2025\n\nYes, I can and it works fine. I was wondering if this is a known issue for some reason on iOS.\n\n## post by david on Oct 1, 2025\n\nNot that I am aware of. There are several IOS apps that connect with Intervals.icu. Maybe some settings in the web view are blocking network calls? The login is just a JSON POST to an Intervals.icu endpoint.\n\n## post by Mark\\_Boulton on Oct 1, 2025\n\nOk thanks. I’ll investigate further and if i fix it i’ll post it back - just in case anyone else experiences it.\n\n## post by Mark\\_Boulton on Oct 1, 2025\n\n4 months later\n\n\n## Split this topic on 23 Jan\n\n## post by Ruud\\_Goorden on 26 Jan\n\n## post by david on 26 Jan"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"The forum confirms Intervals' scope families (`ACTIVITY, WELLNESS, CALENDAR, LIBRARY, SETTINGS`) — so the scope *names* exist at Intervals, which pins down the real mechanism for symptom 2: the tricoach OAuth client is only permitted its registered scope set (the one that worked in September); when the calendar sync made the authorize request ask for `CALENDAR:*` scopes that the client isn't registered for, Intervals answers the authorize step itself with `400 invalid_request` — exactly what the capture shows (state/redirect_uri variations don't matter; the changed parameter is the scope). I have all three causes now. Let me set up the work plan:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_r7bnACeNwoBwdLxAh0Z3Niqe","function":{"name":"TodoList","arguments":"{\"todos\":[{\"title\":\"Fix SPA Connect button (fetch authorize URL, then navigate)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"title\":\"Fix SCOPES in config.py (drop unregistered CALENDAR scopes)\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"title\":\"Fix token expiry handling (Intervals tokens don't expire; no refresh grant)\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"title\":\"Build local fake Intervals.icu + end-to-end verification\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"title\":\"Write ANSWER.md with causes\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"title\":\"Clean up test scaffolding, final checks\",\"status\":\"pending\"}]}"}}]}
